  "body": "**Found in a PathPilot Hub run (770MX sim, v2.14.4, 2026-11-12).** The Tormach golden `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach/drill_peck.nc` (and its inch twin) alarms at line 9:\n\n```\nG73: Cannot feed with zero feed rate\n  in drill_peck_inch.nc: line 9: G73 X0.7874 Y0.3937 Z-0.9449 R0 Q0.7087\n```\n\n**Cause.** The golden is posted from the CL fixture `drill_peck.cl`. Its `; CYCLE Peck ...` record has no feed, and the fixture has no tool record. `CycleRec::props` passes `FeedRate: null`. `tormach.cps` `onCycle` then calls `fw(p.FeedRate)`, which writes nothing, and posts a G73 with no F. The same fixtures also post no `T.. M6`, `S..` or `M3`. So `contour_plate_with_hole.nc` cuts its G1/G2/G3 moves with the spindle never started. In Hub that showed as T0 and spindle 0 rpm, and it still ran to M30.\n\n**Why it matters.** A real CamCraft program carries the tool's feed and spindle, so this has not been seen from the GUI. But the post fails open. Under the Prime Directive, a stream that asks for a feed cycle without a feed, or for a cut with no spindle on, should be refused by name and not posted. On a control that keeps a modal F from an earlier block, a missing F on a canned cycle drills at whatever feed was last in force.\n\n**Done means:**\n- `tormach.cps`, and every post with the same `fw()` pattern on cycles, refuses a canned cycle whose `FeedRate` is missing or not positive, by name.\n- A feed move (G1/G2/G3, or a cycle) before any spindle start is refused by name. Spindleless dialects (plasma, laser) are exempt.\n- The golden fixtures that post to Tormach state a tool, spindle and feed, so the Tormach goldens are real runnable programs. The goldens are regenerated, and the change is listed in the PR.\n- Pinning tests: a cycle with no feed is refused; a cut with no spindle start is refused.\n\nHub evidence: the user's screenshots, 2026-11-12 19:43-19:47.\n",
